&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign helps enable the security, stability, and resiliency of the internet. We are a trusted provider of internet infrastructure services for the networked world and deliver unmatched performance in domain name system (DNS) services.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a mission focused, values driven company where each individual can contribute to building a stronger, more secure internet.&amp;nbsp; We offer a dynamic and flexible work environment with competitive benefits and the ability to grow your career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We appreciate your interest in our company. By joining our Talent Community, our recruiters will know you’re interested in learning about future positions. Please take a moment to submit your resume and answer a few questions below.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign is an equal opportunity employer. That means we recruit, hire, compensate, train, promote, transfer, and administer all terms and conditions of employment without regard to their race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, protected veteran status, disability, or other protected categories under applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional Information:&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/en_US/company-information/verisign-careers/index.xhtml?dmn=verisign.careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Careers Page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/careers/benefits/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Benefits Summary&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/about-us/verisign-cares/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Verisign in the Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/assets/Equal-Employment-Opportunity.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our EEO Statement&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/legal-center/privacy/privacy-job-applicants/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Privacy Notice for Job Applicants/Candidates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/en_US/company-information/verisign-careers/index.xhtml?loc=en_US#:~:text=Reasonable%20Accommodations%20for%20Those%20With%20Disabilities&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Reasonable Accommodations&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Staffing agency policy: No fees will be paid for unsolicited resumes submitted to Verisign or our employees by third parties.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign helps enable the security, stability, and resiliency of the internet. We are a trusted provider of internet infrastructure services for the networked world and deliver unmatched performance in domain name system (DNS) services.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a mission focused, values driven company where each individual can contribute to building a stronger, more secure internet.&amp;nbsp; We offer a dynamic and flexible work environment with competitive benefits and the ability to grow your career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We appreciate your interest in our company. By joining our Talent Community, our recruiters will know you’re interested in learning about future positions. Please take a moment to submit your resume and answer a few questions below.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign is an equal opportunity employer. That means we recruit, hire, compensate, train, promote, transfer, and administer all terms and conditions of employment without regard to their race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, protected veteran status, disability, or other protected categories under applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional Information:&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/en_US/company-information/verisign-careers/index.xhtml?dmn=verisign.careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Careers Page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/careers/benefits/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Benefits Summary&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/about-us/verisign-cares/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Verisign in the Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/assets/Equal-Employment-Opportunity.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our EEO Statement&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/legal-center/privacy/privacy-job-applicants/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Privacy Notice for Job Applicants/Candidates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/en_US/company-information/verisign-careers/index.xhtml?loc=en_US#:~:text=Reasonable%20Accommodations%20for%20Those%20With%20Disabilities&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Reasonable Accommodations&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Staffing agency policy: No fees will be paid for unsolicited resumes submitted to Verisign or our employees by third parties.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign helps enable the security, stability, and resiliency of the internet. We are a trusted provider of internet infrastructure services for the networked world and deliver unmatched performance in domain name system (DNS) services.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a mission focused, values driven company where each individual can contribute to building a stronger, more secure internet.&amp;nbsp; We offer a dynamic and flexible work environment with competitive benefits and the ability to grow your career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign is seeking an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Privileged Access Management (PAM) Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to design, implement, administer, and enhance enterprise privileged access and identity security solutions. This hands-on technical role will focus on PAM engineering, Microsoft Entra ID administration, automation, application integrations, and operational support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate has deep experience with enterprise PAM technologies such as BeyondTrust, strong Microsoft Entra ID expertise, and a solid understanding of IAM, identity governance, authentication, and access security. This individual will partner with security, infrastructure, application, and architecture teams to deliver secure, scalable, and reliable identity solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, configure, administer, and maintain enterprise PAM solutions, in BeyondTrust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer and enhance Microsoft Entra ID, including enterprise applications, authentication, Conditional Access, role-based access control (RBAC), Privileged Identity Management (PIM), MFA, and SSO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onboard applications, privileged accounts, service accounts, and other identities into PAM platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and maintain privileged account policies, credential management, password rotation, session management, and access controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate PAM solutions with enterprise applications, directories, identity platforms, and infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer and support integrations across PAM, IAM, IGA, MFA, and SSO technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scripts and automation to streamline account onboarding, provisioning, testing, monitoring, and other identity-related processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement automated testing and validation where appropriate to improve reliability and deployment efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support privileged access reviews, access certifications, and remediation activities to meet security, audit, and compliance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with security architects and engineering teams to develop technical designs and implement security controls based on least privilege and Zero Trust principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate new PAM and identity technologies and recommend improvements that strengthen security and operational efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain technical documentation, including system configurations, architecture diagrams, integration designs, operational procedures, and troubleshooting guides&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate throughout the solution lifecycle, including design, development, testing, deployment, production support, upgrades, and ongoing maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Information Technology, Cybersecurity, or a related field, or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in PAM, IAM, identity security, security engineering, or related technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of hands-on experience implementing and administering enterprise PAM platforms in BeyondTrust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience administering Microsoft Entra ID in an enterprise environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Entra ID capabilities including Conditional Access, RBAC, PIM, MFA, SSO, enterprise applications, and identity/access management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of PAM concepts, including privileged account management, credential vaulting, password rotation, session management, least privilege, and privileged access controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating PAM solutions with directories, applications, servers, cloud platforms, and other enterprise technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with scripting and automation using technologies such as PowerShell, Python, REST APIs, or similar tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of authentication, authorization, identity lifecycle management, and security best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting audit and compliance requirements, including Sarbanes-Oxley (SOX) controls, preferably in a high-tech environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in our Reston, VA office and offers a hybrid work schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay range is $135,800 - $183,800.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The anticipated annual base salary range for this position is noted above, however, base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, experience. Verisign offers a discretionary bonus which is based on individual and company performance, and certain roles may be eligible for discretionary stock awards.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign is an equal opportunity employer. That means we recruit, hire, compensate, train, promote, transfer, and administer all terms and conditions of employment without regard to their race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, protected veteran status, disability, or other protected categories under applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional Information:&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/en_US/company-information/verisign-careers/index.xhtml?dmn=verisign.careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Careers Page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/careers/benefits/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Benefits Summary&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/about-us/verisign-cares/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Verisign in the Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/assets/Equal-Employment-Opportunity.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our EEO Statement&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/legal-center/privacy/privacy-job-applicants/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Privacy Notice for Job Applicants/Candidates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/en_US/company-information/verisign-careers/index.xhtml?loc=en_US#:~:text=Reasonable%20Accommodations%20for%20Those%20With%20Disabilities&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Reasonable Accommodations&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Staffing agency policy: No fees will be paid for unsolicited resumes submitted to Verisign or our employees by third parties.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign helps enable the security, stability, and resiliency of the internet. We are a trusted provider of internet infrastructure services for the networked world and deliver unmatched performance in domain name system (DNS) services.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a mission focused, values driven company where each individual can contribute to building a stronger, more secure internet.&amp;nbsp; We offer a dynamic and flexible work environment with competitive benefits and the ability to grow your career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are building a new engineering team responsible for establishing and operating the company&#39;s on-premises Artificial Intelligence and Large Language Model (LLM) platform. The Principal Engineer will serve as the senior technical authority for the platform and will help define how AI capabilities are safely, reliably, and effectively implemented throughout the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on technical leadership position. The successful candidate will combine strong systems and infrastructure engineering skills with practical knowledge of modern LLMs, inference platforms, developer tooling, and AI-assisted workflows in an enterprise environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Principal Engineer will have substantial influence over architecture, technology selection, engineering standards, operational practices, and the long-term technical direction of the platform. This must be accomplished while continuing the Protect / Grow / Manage framework that guides the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the principal technical authority for the company&#39;s on-premises AI and LLM architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, operate, and evolve production LLM inference platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and recommend models, inference engines, developer tools, agent frameworks and supporting technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop repeatable evaluation methodologies for determining model quality, performance, reliability and suitability for company workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Information Security teams to design secure mechanisms for applying LLMs to proprietary source code, internal data, documentation, and analytical workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and work with engineering teams to create the most appropriate AI-assisted software engineering capabilities. This includes coding agents, tool use, repository integration, retrieval systems, and related developer workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance existing engineering practices and update them to perform, model deployment, upgrades, rollback, observability, capacity planning and incident response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with security and infrastructure teams to establish appropriate controls for sensitive corporate information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate emerging AI technologies and distinguish technologies suitable for production use from experimental or immature approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype new capabilities and convert successful experiments into reliable production services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other engineers on the AI platform team and provide technical leadership across organizational boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with internal users to identify high-value applications for AI, including software development, data analysis, automation, and knowledge retrieval&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Telecommunications, or related field or equivalent experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years computer engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience designing, operating or troubleshooting complex production systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Linux systems engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of distributed systems, networking, storage, containers, and modern infrastructure platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with modern software development practices, source control, CI/CD, automation, and infrastructure-as-code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming or scripting ability in languages such as Python, Go, C/C++ or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience deploying LLMs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of LLM inference concepts including context windows, tokenization, quantization, batching, concurrency, memory requirements, and accelerator utilization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead major technical initiatives without requiring direct personnel management authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in several of the following areas is desirable. Expertise in every area is not expected.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GPU or accelerator-based computing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LLM inference engines such as llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama, TensorRT-LLM or similar technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes or other container orchestration platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), embeddings, vector search, and enterprise knowledge retrieval&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agentic AI systems, tool-calling models, coding agents, or Model Context Protocol (MCP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-assisted software development environments and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model evaluation, benchmarking, and automated evaluation frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open-weight LLM deployment and model lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise authentication, authorization, secrets management, and audit systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working in environments with strict security, privacy, reliability or regulatory requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security and Responsible AI Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Security and governance are central to this role. The AI Enablement Engineer will be expected to help technical teams adopt AI capabilities in a manner that protects company data, aligns with approved use policies, and supports responsible AI practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;This includes understanding how AI tools interact with sensitive information, how access to AI capabilities should be controlled, and how technical users can safely incorporate AI into engineering workflows. The role requires a strong security mindset and the ability to work closely with governance, security, and platform stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in our Reston, VA office and offers a hybrid work schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay range is $180,700 - $244,500. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The anticipated annual base salary range for this position is noted above, however, base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, experience. Verisign offers a discretionary bonus which is based on individual and company performance, and certain roles may be eligible for discretionary stock awards.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign is an equal opportunity employer. That means we recruit, hire, compensate, train, promote, transfer, and administer all terms and conditions of employment without regard to their race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, protected veteran status, disability, or other protected categories under applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional Information:&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/en_US/company-information/verisign-careers/index.xhtml?dmn=verisign.careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Careers Page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/careers/benefits/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Benefits Summary&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/about-us/verisign-cares/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Verisign in the Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/assets/Equal-Employment-Opportunity.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our EEO Statement&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/legal-center/privacy/privacy-job-applicants/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Privacy Notice for Job Applicants/Candidates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/en_US/company-information/verisign-careers/index.xhtml?loc=en_US#:~:text=Reasonable%20Accommodations%20for%20Those%20With%20Disabilities&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Reasonable Accommodations&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Staffing agency policy: No fees will be paid for unsolicited resumes submitted to Verisign or our employees by third parties.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign helps enable the security, stability, and resiliency of the internet. We are a trusted provider of internet infrastructure services for the networked world and deliver unmatched performance in domain name system (DNS) services.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a mission focused, values driven company where each individual can contribute to building a stronger, more secure internet.&amp;nbsp; We offer a dynamic and flexible work environment with competitive benefits and the ability to grow your career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Principal Engineer is responsible for developing, managing, and optimizing the organization’s global Internet interconnection strategy. This role oversees settlement-free peering, paid peering, IP transit, Internet Exchange (IX) participation, traffic engineering, routing policy, and strategic relationships with network operators, content providers, cloud providers, carriers, and Regional Internet Registries (RIRs).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate possesses strong technical networking expertise, business negotiation skills, and industry engagement experience to improve network performance, reduce transit costs, increase resiliency, and support the company’s global connectivity objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interconnection Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute the global peering and interconnection strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to expand peering relationships and optimize transit utilization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive network growth through strategic partnerships with ISPs, cloud providers, content networks, CDNs, carriers, and hyperscalers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate new IX opportunities and regional expansion initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish KPIs for traffic offload, cost reduction, latency improvements, and resiliency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Peering Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and manage:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Settlement-Free Peering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bilateral Peering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multilateral Peering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public Peering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Peering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain peering policies and qualification requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships through:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PeeringDB&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IX communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry forums&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network operator groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate onboarding and operational support for new peers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve peering disputes, routing issues, and traffic imbalances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internet Exchange (IX) Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage participation across global Internet Exchanges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate IX performance and ROI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate provisioning of:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-connects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Port upgrades&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New exchange deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop business cases for new IX expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain relationships with IX operators and executive leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IP Transit Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage global transit providers and carrier relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct transit capacity planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate contracts and pricing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate transit performance and redundancy requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strategies to reduce transit costs through increased peering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor traffic shifts between transit and peering environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Routing &amp;amp; Traffic Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain routing policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize traffic flows across:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Peering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IX fabrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private interconnections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage traffic engineering initiatives using:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BGP communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Local Preference&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MED&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AS Path Prepending&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze traffic patterns and forecast growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve latency, packet loss, and path optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the company at:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NANOG&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RIPE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;APRICOT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LACNIC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ARIN&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;APNIC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global Peering Forum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build executive-level relationships across the Internet ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in policy discussions and industry working groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor industry trends affecting interconnection and Internet governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Leaderships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
