&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign helps enable the security, stability, and resiliency of the internet. We are a trusted provider of internet infrastructure services for the networked world and deliver unmatched performance in domain name system (DNS) services.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a mission focused, values driven company where each individual can contribute to building a stronger, more secure internet.&amp;nbsp; We offer a dynamic and flexible work environment with competitive benefits and the ability to grow your career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Product Management Director – Top-Level Domains (TLDs), leads the strategic thinking and planning in the areas of core business requirements. This position oversees broad-based cross-functional efforts to direct the design, launch and management of new or enhanced products and services.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position will work closely with the platform, technology services, customer support, finance, legal, marketing and account management teams to ensure that Verisign achieves its business objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key responsibilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drives TLD product strategy. Owns the concept lifecycle from ideation to final approval.&amp;nbsp; Drives approved business plans and concepts to completion as the subject matter expert.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides thought leadership based on feedback gathered from cross-functional teams and reporting potential implications to the product strategy. &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creates and executes roadmaps to achieve business objectives on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively develops strategic assessments of opportunities, providing recommendations to address them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writes reports, situational analyses and training materials through collaboration with peers and cross functional stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years’ experience with generic Top-Level Domains (TLDs), managing products and services and their delivery preferably within a technology-related, regulated industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years’ experience in launching TLDs and managing the TLD lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in business, marketing or a related field, or equivalent experience, required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or equivalent graduate degree, preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, communications, and presentation skills, with the ability to engage effectively with stakeholders, engineers, and senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated and proactive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate at an operational and strategic level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen, good judgment, attention to detail, objectivity, and accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to think both analytically and creatively, making data-informed decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate and communicate effectively in a matrixed environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage a large number of internal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal and influencing skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation abilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
