&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign helps enable the security, stability, and resiliency of the internet. We are a trusted provider of internet infrastructure services for the networked world and deliver unmatched performance in domain name system (DNS) services.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a mission focused, values driven company where each individual can contribute to building a stronger, more secure internet.&amp;nbsp; We offer a dynamic and flexible work environment with competitive benefits and the ability to grow your career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The mission of the Security Architecture Team is to define and advance secure, resilient architecture across Verisign’s systems, networks, applications, cloud platforms, data environments, and emerging technologies. The team combines deep technical expertise with enterprise strategy to reduce risk, enable innovation, and establish security patterns that scale across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have an exciting opportunity for a Senior Information Security Architect. This senior individual-contributor role shapes enterprise security strategy, reference architectures, standards, and technical requirements across the entire company. The architect will lead high-impact design decisions, resolve complex cross-domain security challenges, and advise engineering and executive leaders on risk, tradeoffs, and long-term technology direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working across security engineering, infrastructure, application development, cloud, data, and AI teams, this role ensures security is built into critical services from concept through implementation in production. The Senior Information Security Architect will authoritatively guide the defense of a diverse hybrid technology ecosystem - safeguarding mission essential on-premises architecture, modern cloud platforms, secure application pipelines, and emerging enterprise AI workloads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define enterprise security architecture strategy, principles, reference architectures, reusable patterns, and multi-year roadmaps across network, endpoint, identity, application, cloud, container, data, and detection and response domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead security architecture engagement for complex, high-risk, and cross-functional programs; translate business objectives, threat intelligence, and risk appetite into scalable technical controls and design requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish architecture and security requirements for AI/ML systems, including secure MLOps, model and data lifecycle protection, identity and authorization, platform isolation, model provenance, monitoring, privacy, and responsible-use guardrails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review generative and agentic AI designs—including retrieval-augmented generation, vector databases, third-party models, APIs, plugins, tools, and autonomous actions—and address controls to mitigate the risks of prompt injection, data leakage, excessive agency, insecure output handling, and AI supply-chain compromise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform threat modeling, architecture reviews, and security design assessments for critical systems and emerging technologies; document risk decisions and guide remediation or compensating controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify systemic gaps in the security posture, develop prioritized recommendations and investment roadmaps, and communicate technical risk and tradeoffs clearly to executive leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate security technologies and vendors, guide proofs of concept, and ensure proposed solutions are interoperable, supportable, measurable, and aligned with strategic architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in computer science, cybersecurity, engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of broad information security experience, including significant experience with security architecture and design for complex enterprise environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise across security architecture and secure networking, cloud, identity (both on premises and cloud), endpoint, application security, data protection, and detection and response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead threat modeling and architecture reviews, and to make consequential technical decisions for high-value or high-availability systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of AI/ML architecture and security, including secure MLOps, model and data governance, generative AI, RAG, AI agents, prompt injection, model supply-chain risk, sensitive-data exposure, access controls, and monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate complex technical risk into clear recommendations for engineering teams, business stakeholders, and executive leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional leadership, facilitation, written communication, and mentoring skills, with a record of influencing decisions without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced experience with vulnerability assessment, security risk analysis, and risk-based prioritization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in application security, secure software development, and the OWASP Top 10 and OWASP Top 10 for Large Language Model Applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing security for public cloud, hybrid environments, infrastructure as code, and CI/CD pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with frameworks such as NIST CSF, NIST AI RMF, MITRE ATT&amp;amp;CK, or MITRE ATLAS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certifications such as CISSP, CCSP, SABSA, or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in our Reston, VA office and offers a hybrid work schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay range is $164,300 - $222,300.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The anticipated annual base salary range for this position is noted above, however, base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, experience. Verisign offers a discretionary bonus which is based on individual and company performance, and certain roles may be eligible for discretionary stock awards.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign is an equal opportunity employer. That means we recruit, hire, compensate, train, promote, transfer, and administer all terms and conditions of employment without regard to their race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, protected veteran status, disability, or other protected categories under applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional Information:&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/en_US/company-information/verisign-careers/index.xhtml?dmn=verisign.careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Careers Page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/careers/benefits/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Benefits Summary&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/about-us/verisign-cares/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Verisign in the Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/assets/Equal-Employment-Opportunity.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our EEO Statement&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/legal-center/privacy/privacy-job-applicants/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Privacy Notice for Job Applicants/Candidates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.verisign.com/en_US/company-information/verisign-careers/index.xhtml?loc=en_US#:~:text=Reasonable%20Accommodations%20for%20Those%20With%20Disabilities&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Reasonable Accommodations&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Staffing agency policy: No fees will be paid for unsolicited resumes submitted to Verisign or our employees by third parties.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign helps enable the security, stability, and resiliency of the internet. We are a trusted provider of internet infrastructure services for the networked world and deliver unmatched performance in domain name system (DNS) services.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a mission focused, values driven company where each individual can contribute to building a stronger, more secure internet.&amp;nbsp; We offer a dynamic and flexible work environment with competitive benefits and the ability to grow your career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign is seeking a Senior Observability Engineer to design and advance observability capability that transforms operational data into actionable insight. This role will create unified, “single pane of glass” experiences that enables executive decision makers, technology leaders, and application teams to understand system health, service performance, customer impact, and operational risks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines deep observability engineering expertise with strong data-analysis and communication skills. They will establish application Service Level Indicators (SLIs), Service Level Objectives (SLOs), dashboards, and analytical models that connect technical performance to business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is part of a highly skilled engineering and infrastructure team responsible for the design, administration, security, and operation of Verisign’s&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture &amp;amp; Infrastructure Services (AIS) Team&lt;/strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp; The position exists to strengthen our operational insights and enable key decision making through analytics. The role requires deep observability expertise combined with strong technical leadership. This individual will focus on improving observability, inherently improving system availability, reliability, and/or scalability of our shared services infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is outcome driven, leads across the stack, navigates the gap between engineering and executive layer, and can context switch seamlessly between executive presentation and all aspects of constructing concise dashboards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Observability and Executive Dashboards:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain unified observability dashboards that consolidates metrics, logs, traces, events, and application/system data with the purview of Architecture and Infrastructure environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop executive-level views of service health, availability, performance, customer impact, operational risk, and capacity trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex technical data into clear insights that support prioritization, risk management, and operational decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define dashboard standards that provide consistent terminology, visualizations, service hierarchies, and health indicators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure dashboards emphasize actionable signals and trends rather than simply displaying large volumes of telemetry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SLO and SLI Engineering:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with application owners, product teams, and business stakeholders to define meaningful SLIs and SLOs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish indicators for availability, latency, throughput, error rates, data quality, user experience, and critical business transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop error-budget policies and reporting that help teams balance reliability, risk, and delivery speed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardize SLO definitions, measurement methods, ownership, and governance across applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate the collection, calculation, visualization, and reporting of SLO performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify services that lack adequate monitoring or reliability targets and develop plans to close those gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data Analysis and Operational Intelligence:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze observability data to identify performance degradation, reliability risks, recurring incidents, capacity constraints, and emerging trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Correlate technical telemetry with customer experience and business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop health scores, trend analyses, anomaly detection, and predictive indicators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform deep-dive analysis to determine the root causes and broader patterns behind incidents and service degradation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce concise operational insights and recommendations for executive and technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure the effectiveness of observability investments using outcomes such as reduced detection time, faster recovery, fewer recurring incidents, and improved SLO attainment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leadership:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior technical authority for observability, monitoring, and reliability measurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop observability strategies, standards, roadmaps, and adoption models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with executives, architects, application teams, site reliability engineers, security teams, and operations leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach engineering teams on instrumentation, dashboard design, SLO development, and data-driven problem-solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical evaluations and make recommendations regarding observability platforms and capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote a culture in which operational decisions are based on measurable service performance and customer impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Requirements:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
