&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has solid understanding of writing software in a system-level programming language (C, C++, Rust)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven foundation in Computer Science fundamentals (data structures, algorithms, operating systems, object-oriented design)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of CI/CD concepts and tools (e.g., Jenkins, Groovy, GitHub)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with or a strong willingness to learn infrastructure automation and platform engineering technologies such as Terraform, Ansible, Puppet and OpenStack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with Linux&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python or similar scripting language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding problem solving and trouble-shooting skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent teammate who enjoys a collaborative team environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relevant Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant work experience in software development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years development in a system-level programming language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working on an Agile software development team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in computer science or related field, or equivalent work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with DNS at the protocol level&lt;/li&gt;
