&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign helps enable the security, stability, and resiliency of the internet. We are a trusted provider of internet infrastructure services for the networked world and deliver unmatched performance in domain name system (DNS) services.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a mission focused, values driven company where each individual can contribute to building a stronger, more secure internet.&amp;nbsp; We offer a dynamic and flexible work environment with competitive benefits and the ability to grow your career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verisign is looking for a Senior Engineer to join the Architecture and Infrastructure Team. In this role the Engineer will be responsible for implementing systems to gather and analyze large data sets representing network/application traffic flows, DNS and Web content data and much more to derive actionable operational and business intelligence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal Engineer is an individual who can bring ideas from all areas, is proactive, has a strong sense of urgency and ownership, and is used to deal with distributed systems, large-scale system design, networking, data storage and security. The successful candidate will support the design, development, integration, testing, deployment, and maintenance of software solutions in a collaborative Agile environment. This role provides an excellent opportunity to gain hands-on experience with modern software engineering practices, including software integration, vulnerability management, automated testing, and CI/CD pipeline development in a big data eco-system. Successful engineers will work closely with team members to master our software and make a positive impact on projects as well as team chemistry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Person:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a highly skilled Senior Engineer who:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply “Big Data” solutions to solve real customer problems using web content and traffic data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, write, test, and maintain object-oriented software for collecting, storing, analyzing and reporting on big data sets, using Java, Python and various open-source technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on systems with enormous data processing requirements and ensure all OLAs and SLAs are comfortably met&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform all aspects of system verification, including all phases of the testing process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with application architects and developers to define test approaches, success criteria, and testing procedures to ensure quality in data, data processing, and interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use industry best practices to deliver high-quality solutions leveraging open-source tools/toolkits and utilities with automated daily builds, tests, and deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively with cross-functional organizations including system architects, project managers, product managers and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a hands-on Engineer and lead by example to earn the respect as an effective technical leader&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of documentation and knowledge sharing across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Takes ownership and responsibility for organizational practices and processes and their continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads incident response across the engineering organization as needed to troubleshoot challenging problems that involve virtual environments, networking, kernel configs, distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s + 12 years OR Masters + 10 years of relevant work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of software development experience in a Unix environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert level programming experience with Java, Python or other equivalent programming language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Big Data (Map reduce, Spark, etc) applications and jobs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Hadoop, Hive, Kafka, Spark and other Big Data Technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with testing systems from existing system and functional specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with performance testing and tuning of big data jobs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in data migration methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with RDBMs, Timeseries DBs and/or NoSQL databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in Linux environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Automation frameworks/systems like Ansible, Terraform, Jenkins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Private or Public Cloud environments and Cloud-native application architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in highly productive team environments employing agile practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in our Reston, VA office and offers a hybrid work schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay range is $164,300 - $222,300.&lt;/p&gt;
